<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Dismember's cast job (HemophageWarcasket.JobDriver_Dismember): the walk to the target,
    the windup, the strike and the drain, under a JobDef of its own because the driver finds
    its ability as the one whose def names this job. reportString is never shown, the driver
    reports the ability's jobReportString, but it is a translatable field.

    checkOverrideOnDamage Never: being hit never interrupts the pilot, who uses this in
    melee. Vanilla considers an override only for a job that is not player-forced, which a
    queued order is not, so the def says it outright.

    neverShowWeapon: the pilot's hands do the work, so the weapon is holstered for the whole
    job, as for vanilla's touch abilities.
  -->
  <JobDef>
    <defName>HPWC_Dismember</defName>
    <driverClass>HemophageWarcasket.JobDriver_Dismember</driverClass>
    <reportString>tearing a limb off TargetA.</reportString>
    <checkOverrideOnDamage>Never</checkOverrideOnDamage>
    <neverShowWeapon>true</neverShowWeapon>
  </JobDef>
</Defs>
